# Carson's model file (contains API key - never commit)
*.xlsm
reference/

# Personal photos stay out of the repo by default — full-resolution originals are
# camera files with EXIF and no business being in git.
#
# The two web-sized headshots below are the exception: the About section is meant
# to be seen, the site is public, and Cloudflare deploys from this repo, so a file
# that is not committed is a 404 on the live site. There is no separate upload step
# (the earlier note here said to upload to the host directly — that was written for
# a different host and was never true of this one).
#
# Keep the masters local and ignored; commit only the 500px JPEGs, which are
# ~66 KB and ~86 KB against 4.1 MB and 2.8 MB.
#
# The masters now live in reference/headshots/, NOT here. wrangler uploads whatever
# sits in frontend/ and does not read this file, so keeping them alongside the
# shipped JPEGs meant every deploy handed Cloudflare two camera originals with their
# EXIF intact. A .assetsignore did not filter them (verified against wrangler
# 4.123 — the file count was unchanged), so the only reliable fix is to keep them
# out of the directory that gets published.
frontend/assets/*.jpg
frontend/assets/*.jpeg
frontend/assets/*.png
frontend/assets/*.webp
frontend/assets/*.gif
!frontend/assets/.gitkeep
!frontend/assets/carson.jpg
!frontend/assets/zoom.jpg

# README screenshots are documentation, not photos — they must ship or the
# README renders a broken image on GitHub.
!frontend/assets/screenshot-*.png